      'Other neighborhoods\' traffic circles have no bearing on what caused the accident drop at this intersection. This question changes the subject rather than testing the argument.',
      'Construction scheduling is irrelevant to safety outcomes. Whether the project finished on time tells us nothing about why accidents fell — this question is non-diagnostic.',
      'Initial driver confusion is a real phenomenon, but knowing about it would not discriminate between the circle and alternative causes of the 40 percent decline. It is at best a side issue, far less diagnostic than the simultaneous-change question.',
      'Correct. This is the key confound question: a "yes" answer supplies rival causes for the accident drop, while a "no" answer isolates the traffic circle. Either way, the answer directly determines the argument\'s strength.',
